PROVES: real CoreAudio integration works end-to-end on Windows.

Production startup issue caught + fixed:
- The W6.42 IAudioStaDispatcher seam refactor introduced a DI registration
  gap. DeviceChangeNotifier requires IAudioStaDispatcher but Program.cs
  only registered the concrete AudioStaDispatcher class. Agent crashed
  at startup with "Unable to resolve service for type IAudioStaDispatcher".
- Fixed by adding services.AddSingleton<IAudioStaDispatcher>(sp =>
  sp.GetRequiredService<AudioStaDispatcher>()) to Program.cs.
- This bug was NOT caught by W6 tests because the test factories
  (StatusEndpointTests, AudioEndpointsTests, etc.) strip hosted services
  via services.Where(d => d.ServiceType == typeof(IHostedService)),
  removing DeviceChangeNotifier from the validated graph.
